   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\">Reminder:  Tomorrow (Friday), Carl Boettiger will present at D-RUG on using ROpenSci packages to retrieve, process, and upload data from online repositories.  See you there!<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div><div style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);border:none;line-height:1.2;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">---</p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);border:none;line-height:1.2;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Hi all,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">This week at D-RUG we’ll have guest speaker <a href=\"http://www.carlboettiger.info/\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,238)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.carlboettiger.info/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468440677000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1yICw3oaX6C5n_dMy7DKzp\">Carl Boettiger</a>, co-founder of <a href=\"http://ropensci.org/\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,238)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ropensci.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468440677000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1TlYMMaJv99n1kS3QLej_c\">ROpenSci</a>.  ROpenSci develops R packages that provide access to a variety of <a href=\"http://ropensci.org/packages/index.html#data_access\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,238)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ropensci.org/packages/index.html%23data_access&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468440677000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2k6XQrrDMcISVGBLOudhW5\">online scientific data repositories</a>, full-text journal articles, and data on scholarly metrics so you can download and analyze these within R.  Carl will talk about some of these packages and walk through how to use them to retrieve, process, and upload data.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Per usual, we’ll be in Wickson 2124. Carl will speak 10-11 and we’ll have open work time 11-12, with Carl around to answer questions.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">For a preview, try out these quick examples of what some ROpenSci packages can do:</p>\r\n</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div style=\"font-size:1em;font-family:Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);border:none;line-height:1.2;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><ul style=\"padding-left:2em;margin:1em 0px\">\r\n<li style=\"margin:1em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Get and map all the observations of a species from the Berkeley Natural History Museum’s EcoEngine database:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;overflow:auto;margin:1em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre-wrap;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">install.packages(&quot;ecoengine&quot;); library(ecoengine)\r\nArtemisia &lt;- ee_observations(scientific_name = &quot;Artemisia douglasiana&quot;)\r\nee_map(Artemisia)\r\n</code></pre></li>\r\n<li style=\"margin:1em 0px\"><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Search across PloS journals:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;overflow:auto;margin:1em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:nowrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre-wrap;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:rgb(248,248,255)\">install.packages(&#39;rplos&#39;); library(rplos)\r\nsearchplos(&#39;Phytophthora ramorum&#39;, c(&#39;id&#39;,&#39;title&#39;), limit = 10)\r\n`\r\n</code></pre></li>\r\n</ul></div></div>"
